        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b28c4a35a5a549e99ed0dffebc7ecd29",
      "statement": "Concurrent first-time certificate generation (pair CLI vs daemon) is made race-safe via O_CREATE|O_EXCL on the private key file; the loser polls for the winner to finish (2-second deadline), and a timeout indicates an orphaned partial generation requiring manual deletion and full re-pairing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/lanauth/lanauth.go#L115-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8e4fb91147448d895cfc76046cce6437ce4090c534d117393204239996c6af85:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/lanauth/lanauth.go#L56-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:72c15ce2eb922eb255fae61fe17ff3f12f6388e38144f78766f3ad14fca43299:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_201c29ad5c0749c991070efd388a4ebc",
      "statement": "Pairing uses a one-time QR secret: herdr-connect pair generates a 32-byte secret and stores only its SHA-256 hash with a 5-minute TTL (PairingSecretTTL); the QR payload carries {v, fp, hosts, port, secret}; the mobile client POSTs {device_name, secret} to /v1/pair, and CompletePairing returns a per-device bearer token exactly once, stored client-side in iOS Keychain. Only hashes of secret and token persist server-side.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/lan-tls-pairing.md#L50-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee9017e6f075d5780f50ea6aa910fe7500efaec2da4c08c6ed64e3740d5dcb1a:"
        },
        {
