          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:671e5f02a74947cc8131adf809f42d94afc30f4cd0e2f785a9610d7a3e83de02:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/lanauth/lanauth.go#L201-L240",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64fbcec013e8a0be818c63d4b547498797ee40aa1b5de6163b6b5c0d4142a873:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_46582d657ffc4c6881c2e214619e0b3f",
      "statement": "store.CompletePairing performs validation and consumption atomically in one SQLite transaction: a conditional UPDATE consumes the secret only if it exists, is unconsumed, and unexpired, then inserts the paired device and links the secret to it; the write-first statement ordering avoids WAL-mode SQLITE_BUSY on lock upgrade, and all invalid-secret causes return the same ok=false to prevent status oracle probing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/lan-tls-pairing.md#L60-L64",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1062a0a781e22924492d36eb9793d2e10a8626237de70366616871b41723b64e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/store/pairing.go#L44-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a1dfc157d2fbc9fa1c3dbc9eb90ee6642e601f718b55bf13560c7b46939871e7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5b828262b1b7423986da15648f34a792",
      "statement": "Every endpoint except /v1/pair requires Authorization Bearer; lanauth.Authenticate returns a three-state result mapped by the HTTP layer: AuthStatusMissing (absent/unknown token or DB error) to 401 unauthorized, AuthStatusRevoked to 401 revoked (distinct so the client can prompt re-pairing), AuthStatusOK touches last_seen_at_ms and the request proceeds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/lan-tls-pairing.md#L74-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5837b29f4e714511f47d2d067ffe7d5f57b0551481d8b395a7b505ee0ce4982e:"
